te shown is the equivalent average rate (bank discount basis) on accepted bids. For details of bill offerings, see Table 2. On September 3, 1963, the Treasury began the monthly issuance of on\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 409, 867, 450], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"year bills to mature on the last day of each month and, in addition, on September 30, 1966, it began the monthly issuance of bills to\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 450, 726, 473], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"mature in nine months.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 473, 657, 494], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"from date of additional issue in case of a reope In reopening, the amount issued is in addition\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 494, 804, 519], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"In reopenings, the amount issued is in addition to the amount of original offering.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 519, 360, 543], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"For securities exc\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 543, 802, 563], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"For price at which issued, see Tables 5 and 6.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 563, 845, 635], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Includes $3,051 million of the 4% notes and $1,076 million of the 4% bonds allotted to Federal Reserve banks and Government investment accounts.\\nExchange offering available to owners of nonmarketable 2-3/4% Treas\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 635, 876, 699], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"bonds, investment Series B-1975-80, dated April 1, 1951. For further information on the original offering see Treasury Bulletin for April 1951, page A-1. Amounts shown are as of November 30, 1967.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 699, 829, 743], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Tax anticipation bill, acceptable at face value in payment of income taxes due on the 15th of the month immediately preceding maturity\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 743, 871, 813], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Payment for subscriptions allotted could be made in cash or in Treasury bonds, notes, or certificates of indebtedness maturing on the issue date of the new security. Consists of allotments paid for with Treasury notes maturing\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 813, 777, 833], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"November 15, 1965\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [139, 833, 867, 1070], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"11/ Subscriptions from States, political subdivisions or instrumentalities thereof, public pension and retirement and other public funds, international organizations in which the United States holds membership, foreign central banks and foreign states, Government investment accounts and the Federal Reserve banks, totaling $7,169 million, were allotted in full where, as provided in the offering circular, the subscriber made the required certification of ownership of notes maturing November 15, 1965. Subscriptions subject to allotment totaled $4,898 million: those up to and including $200,000 were allotted in full; all others were allotted 48 percent but in no case less than $200,000.\\n12/ Subscriptions for $50,000 or less were allotted in full.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 1070, 867, 1113], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"for more than $50,000 were allotted 14.5 percent but 