953, Treasury bond yields are reported to the Treasury by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York, based on closing bid quotations in the over-the-counter market. Yields for prior periods were computed on the basis of mean of closing bid and ask quotations. Moody's Investor Service is the source for the average of Aaa corporate bonds.\\n1/ Series includes bonds on which the interest income is subject to\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [951, 1869, 1702, 2042], \"page_id\": 83}], \"content\": \"normal tax and surtax which are neither due nor callable before a given number of years as follows: April 1953 to date, 10 years; April 1952 - March 1953, 12 years; October 1941 - March 1952, 15 years. For bonds currently in the series, see Table 3 under \\\"Market Quotations on Treasury Securities\\\" in this issue of the Bulletin.\\n2/ One or more new long-term bonds added to the average (see footnote 1).\\n3/ An existing bond dropped from the average (see footnote 1).\\n4/ Market closed.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [2168, 1407, 2206, 1682], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [622, 162, 1833, 233], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"AVERAGE YIELDS OF LONG-TERM TREASURY AND CORPORATE BONDS Monthly Series 1/\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [2168, 139, 2206, 178], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"3L\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [239, 256, 2091, 1600], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [2121, 601, 2142, 1230], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"AVERAGE YIELDS OF LONG-TERM BONDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1998, 1628, 2062, 1647], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"F-676-A\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [249, 1628, 453, 1645], \"page_id\": 84}], \"content\": \"Office of the Secretary of the Treasury\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 95, 409, 131], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"December 1967\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1651, 111, 1682, 136], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"79\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [581, 152, 1207, 177], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"INTERNATIONAL FINANCIAL STATISTICS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [147, 260, 874, 463], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"The tables in this section are designed to provide data on United States reserve assets and liabilities and other statistics related to the United States balance of payments and international financial position. A number of changes were introduced in the May 1967 Bulletin to increase the usefulness of this section.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 494, 878, 849], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"Table 1 has been revised to include in the reserve assets of the United States its reserve position in the International Monetary Fund. In accordance with Fund policies the United States has the right to draw foreign currencies equivalent to this amount virtually automatically if needed. (Under appropriate conditions the United States could draw additional amounts equal to the United States quota of $5,160 million.) This revised presentation corresponds to the treatment of United States monetary reserves in the United States balance of payments accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [145, 874, 880, 1044], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"Table 2 brings together the various statistical components of the liabilities which enter into the United States balance of payments calculated on the liquidity basis. The inclusion of the United States reserve position in the International Monetary Fund in Table 1 requires that the \\\"holdings of\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [939, 257, 1667, 391], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"dollars\\\" of the Fund be excluded from the data on liabilities to foreigners, in order to avoid double counting. For further explanation of this change in the liabilities statistics, see headnote to \\\"Capital Movements\\\" section.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [937, 419, 1669, 594], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"Table 3 (formerly Table 5), presenting an area breakdown of United States liquid liabilities to official institutions of foreign countries, has been revised to include holdings of convertible nonmarketable United States Government securities with an original maturity of more than one year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [943, 615, 1669, 712], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"Table 4 (formerly Table 2) is virtually unchanged and shows United States Treasury nonmarketable bonds and notes issued to official institutions of foreign countries.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [943, 743, 1667, 802], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"Table 5 sets forth the factors which affect the United States position in the International Monetary Fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [945, 836, 1671, 1049], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"Table 6 (formerly Table 3) presents United States net monetary gold transactions with foreign countries and inter-national and regional organizations. The former Table 4, which presented the estimated gold reserves and dollar holdings of foreign countries and international institutions, was discontinued in the May 1967 Bulletin.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [346, 1121, 1479, 1178], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"Table 1. - U.S. Reserve Assets: Gold Stock, Holdings of Convertible Foreign Currencies, and Reserve Position in the International Monetary Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [779, 1206, 1019, 1229], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [139, 1237, 1694, 1900], \"page_id\": 85}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>End of calendar year or month</th><th>Total reserve assets</th><th colspan=\\\"2\\\">Gold stock 1/</th><th>Convertible foreign currencies 3/</th><th>Reserve position in International Monetary Fund 4/</th></tr><tr><th></th><th></th><th>Total 2/</th><th>Treasury</th><th></th><th></th></tr><tr><td>1957</td><td>24,832</td><td>22,857</td><td>22,781</td><td>-</td><td>1,975</td></tr><tr><td>1958</td><td>22,540</td><td>20,582</td><td>20,534</td><td>-</td><td>1,958</td></tr><tr><td>1959</td><td>21,504</td><td>19,507</td><td>19,456</td><td>-</td><td>1,997</td></tr><tr><td>1960</td><td>19,359</td><td>17,804</td><td>17,767</td><td>-</td><td>1,555</td></tr><tr><td>1961</td><td>18,753</td><td>16,947</td><td>16,889</td><td>116</td><td>1,690</td></tr><tr><td>1962</td><td>17,220</td><td>16,057</td><td>15,978</td><td>99</td><td>1,064</td></tr><tr><td>1963</td><td>16,843</td><td>15,596</td><td>15,513</td><td>212</td><td>1,035</td></tr><tr><td>1964</td><td>16,672</td><td>15,471</td><td>15,388</td><td>432</td><td>769</td></tr><tr><td>1965</td><td>15,450</td><td>13,806 5/</td><td>13,733 5/</td><td>781</td><td>863 5/</td></tr><tr><td>1966</td><td>14,882</td><td>13,235</td><td>13,159</td><td>1,321</td><td>326</td></tr><tr><t