ontent\": \"5/ Includes foreign currency assets, representing loans and other\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [988, 319, 1678, 633], \"page_id\": 155}], \"content\": \"receivables recoverable in foreign currency as well as balances of foreign currencies in United States depositaries, aggregating $7,517 million in dollar equivalent. These currencies, acquired primarily without the payment of dollars, were generated under various Government programs, principally the Agricultural Trade Development and Assistance Act of 1954, as amended, and the Mutual Security Acts, as amended. Dollar equivalents are computed for reporting purposes, to provide a common denominator for the currencies of the many countries involved. Foreign currencies on hand and on deposit and loans under section 104 (e) of the Agricultural Trade Development and Assistance Act of 1954, as amended, are stated at the rates as of June 30, 1967, at which the United States could purchase currencies on the market for regular operating purposes. Other loans are stated at the rates at which they are to be repaid or at rates in effect when the loans were extended. Currencies that are dollar denominated or guaranteed as to rate of exchange are stated at rates specified in the agreements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [775, 656, 1060, 681], \"page_id\": 155}], \"content\": \"Footnotes to Table 2\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 692, 438, 717], \"page_id\": 155}], \"content\": \"1/ See Table 1, footnote 4.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 717, 869, 759], \"page_id\": 155}], \"content\": \"2/ Foreign currency assets are included throughout the table (see Table 1, footnote 5).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 759, 884, 877], \"page_id\": 155}]